### [CLI_TOOL_PREFERENCES]

Use modern Rust-based replacements over legacy tools when available:

| Legacy | Modern | Why |
|--------|--------|-----|
| `grep` | `rg` | Ripgrep - blazing fast, respects .gitignore |
| `find` | `fd` | Intuitive syntax, `fd pattern` |
| `du` | `dust` | Visual tree of disk usage |
| `df` | `duf` | User-friendly disk table with colors |
| `top`/`htop` | `btm` | Bottom - customizable dashboard |
| `sed` | `sd` | Modern regex, no escaping hell |
| `curl` | `xh` | HTTPie-like with JSON formatting |
| `cat` | `bat` | Syntax highlighting, line numbers |
| `ls` | `eza` | Modern with icons, git status |
| `cd` + `ls` | `zoxide` | Smart cd with fuzzy matching |
| `git diff` | `delta` | Syntax-highlighting, VS Code-like |

For project tasks, prefer `mise run <task>` over `make <target>` when `.mise.toml` exists.

